WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
- Well, I have to go to this
one because "Hands Clean,"

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.020
I've actually covered that on this show.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.040
I know, right?
(audience laughing)

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.720
I know, I know.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.580
I get that gasp.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.000
But it's the things you talk about.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.895
They're just so poignant.

00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:15.660
Like people, they don't
know how to word it.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.517
And you have this very amazing way

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.920
of saying what we really wanna say

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.296
or we don't know how to
identify it, and "Hands Clean,"

00:00:23.296 --> 00:00:26.190
I mean, that's a really rough song.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.680
Is that from like childhood trauma and on?

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:29.910
- Mm-hmm.
- Gah!

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.620
- Yeah, young teen-
- There's a lot

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.330
in those lyrics.
- Yes.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.320
And when I first wrote it,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.067
I remember the record company having said,

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:38.460
"Let's do this video where it's a karaoke

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.110
and there's kids and it's joy."

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.407
And I asked them, I said,
"Have you heard the song?"

00:00:42.407 --> 00:00:43.980
(audience laughing)

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.450
And they said, "Yeah, it's great."

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.370
I was like, "Okay, so you
haven't heard the song.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.900
Alright."
- Oh!

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.530
- It just felt like this
incongruent kind of thing.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.810
But it actually was a lovely way

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.370
to present a song that otherwise

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.740
might not have even been
listened to, I think.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.180
- Absolutely. That's what I'm saying.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.830
You have this very catchy way,

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.810
but bringing your like, (chuckles)

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.535
Webster dictionary words...

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:06.510
(all laughing)
I'm like...

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.280
Do you know that? This is not a lie.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.220
I bought my first
dictionary because of you.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.446
- I didn't know what I was talking about.

00:01:13.446 --> 00:01:14.566
(audience applauding)

00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:15.840
- I was like, I dunno how
old. I was very young.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.900
And I was like, "What are these words?

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.510
They mean something and I
just need to look them up."

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.090
And literally, you are the
reason why I owned a dictionary

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.230
for the very first time.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.140
But you are, you're such
a great teacher in that

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.610
and you're very clever at putting it

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.980
in such a pop like rock like element

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.990
to where it's catchy
enough in the pop way,

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.880
but it's rock and
alternative and raw enough

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.740
that it's like cool and indie.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.990
Like, I don't think anybody's ever

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.370
done you.
- Bridged those worlds?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.203
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:42.203 --> 00:01:43.710
I don't think, and since then.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.350
- Well, it's a combination
of love for the entertainment

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.150
and the presentation and the performance

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:48.983
which I live for.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:51.720
And then I also live for the not precious,

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:55.800
dirty birdy, just go for it
and don't worry about it.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:56.760
Don't censor.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.890
So a nice combination is my fantasy.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.930
- I love that it's uncensored. Ugh!

